{{also|Diaspora|diasporă|diaspóra|diáspora}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|Diaspora}} {{qualifier|in certain senses}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*sper-}}
From {{bor|en|grc|διασπορᾱ́|t=dispersion}}, from {{m|grc|διασπείρω|t=to scatter}}, from {{m|grc|δια-|pos=prefix indicating motion across or in all directions}} + {{m|grc|σπείρω|t=to sow}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/daɪˈæs.pə.ɹə/|/daɪˈæs.pɹə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/daɪˈæs.pɚ.ə/|/daɪˈæs.pɹə/|/diˈæs.pɚ.ə/|/diˈæs.pɹə/|a=GA}}<ref>{{R:MWO}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com}}</ref>
** {{audio|en|En-us-diaspora.ogg|a=GA}}
* {{hyphenation|en|di|a|spo|ra}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|diasporae|diasporai}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} The [[dispersion]] of the [[Jews]] among the [[Gentile]]s after the Babylonian [[captivity]] (6th century {{BCE}}).
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Any similar [[dispersion]].
#: {{ux|en|The African '''diaspora''' caused a melding of cultures, both African cultures and Western ones, in many places.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023 July 12|author=Paul Clifton|title=Network News: Saved: Trust protects Adrian Shooter's legacy|journal=RAIL|issue=987|page=29|text=We're going to use her to train young people in the skills of maintaining these machines, and encourage the Indian '''diaspora''' in this country to get involved in our hobby of steam railways.}}
# {{lb|en|collective}} A group so dispersed, especially Jews outside of the land of [[Israel]].
# The regions where such a dispersed group (especially the Jews) resides, taken collectively.
#: {{ux|en|Jews in the '''diaspora''' often have a different perspective on anti-Semitism from Israeli Jews.}}
# Any dispersion of an originally [[homogeneous]] [[entity]], such as a [[language]] or [[culture]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=New Englishes: the case of Singapore|page=1|author=Joseph Foley|year=1988|passage=Small wonder that there should have been in recent years fresh talk of the '''diaspora''' of English into several mutually incomprehensible languages}}

